        "description": "",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>fptf-flipbook-converter.zip</code> file via WordPress ? Plugins ? Add New ? Upload Plugin</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin</li>\n<li>Open the <strong>PDF TO FLIPBOOK</strong> menu in the dashboard</li>\n<li>Upload your PDF</li>\n<li>Copy the generated shortcode and paste it into any page or post</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"how%20do%20i%20add%20a%20flipbook%20to%20a%20page%3F\">\nHow do I add a flipbook to a page?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Upload your PDF and copy the generated shortcode into any post or page.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20work%20on%20mobile%20devices%3F\">\nDoes it work on mobile devices?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Flipbooks are fully responsive and touch-friendly.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"are%20links%20inside%20the%20pdf%20clickable%3F\">\nAre links inside the PDF clickable?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. All PDF hyperlinks are automatically detected and clickable inside the flipbook.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20use%20external%20services%20or%20apis%3F\">\nDoes it use external services or APIs?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Everything runs locally on your server.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20customize%20the%20design%3F\">\nCan I customize the design?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. You can customize styles with CSS and adjust settings from the plugin.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added clickable PDF links support</li>\n<li>Improved rendering accuracy</li>\n<li>UI improvements</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added upload from Media Library</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Performance optimizations</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added custom post type support</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added shadow gradient</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
